From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:20:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a pipeline library's Metal
 libraries build in the background

A pipeline library's vertex or fragment shader compiled on its own now
makes its MSL in vkCreateGraphicsPipelines (NIR lowering, passes and
nir_to_msl: 4-14 ms on the phone) and queues its Metal library, which
took 0.2-1 s each, 97-99% of the library's time (PLA-437 step 1). The
device's queue builds them one at a time, oldest first, on a thread of
its own at utility QoS on Apple systems, started with the first one: the
phone's Metal compiler service runs about two builds at once, and this
leaves the other to the builds draws wait for. Portal 2 creates about
600 libraries at a chapter load, most of which its draws never use, and
its draws waited for them behind DXVK's compile threads.

A link whose libraries are not built yet does not wait: it compiles the
whole pipeline, as flag-off does, keyed by all of the draw's state and
kept, and counts "library-pending" as its fallback ([kk-compile] link
full fallback=library-pending); the pair is not marked unfit, so later
draws link it apart once both are built. The libraries it needs move to
the queue's front. A library whose build failed falls back the same way
(vertex-library, fragment-library).

Each queued build keeps a copy of the shader's packed MSL and a
reference held by its source and one by the queue while queued or
building. A source destroyed while its library is queued takes it off
the queue unbuilt; one destroyed while it builds leaves the library to
be released when it is built. Device finish drops what is queued and
waits for the build in progress. Serializing a library shader still
writes its MSL (the Metal library was never serialized), so a later
launch deserializes it and builds its Metal library at once, as before.
Deserialized libraries and the empty fragment shader's are built at once.

MESA_KK_DEBUG=sync_libraries builds them in vkCreateGraphicsPipelines as
before, for A/B. With MESA_KK_DEBUG=compile, a queued library's
gpl-phases line ends with queue_ms, its time in the queue; a dropped
one logs "[kk-compile] gpl <kind> dropped queued|building"; and the
link totals are followed by "[kk-compile] gpl-queue": libraries queued,
built, failed, dropped, moved to the front and waiting. Without
MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl there is no queue and no thread, and nothing
changes.

Linear: PLA-437
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-22-kk-gpl-cold-cache.md
Offered-upstream: no
